The application source branch and the configuration repository's promotion branches belong to different repositories. Record their commits and review results separately.

The latest reference gives different promotion paths for different contexts. Its template-release procedure uses `develop` → `main`, while the review-and-promotion summary states `development` → `staging` → `main`. Confirm the configuration repository's active branch rules before opening a request PR.

Initial enrollment triggers the initial build routes. Later source changes trigger the configured recurring builds. The selected template determines which steps run for each route and their order. Confirm that the configured security gate evaluates the completed assessment before reporting a security pass. The latest reference describes High/Critical findings as blocking and Medium findings as requiring remediation within 30 days. Store delivery follows its own configured route and approvals.

## 3. Know the tools

| Tool | What it does | Where you use it |
|---|---|---|
| GitHub Enterprise | Stores source and configuration, and hosts pull requests. | Your Mac and the repository website. |
| Vela | Validates enrollment requests and runs protected platform automation. | Configuration-repository PR checks and platform runs. |
| Bitrise | Runs the approved mobile build workflows. | Build pages, step logs, and artifact results. |
| Danger | Adds automated feedback to pull requests. | PR comments and configured check results. |
| Sauce Labs | Runs prepared device tests and collects execution evidence. | Testing results and the device-testing guide. |
| NowSecure | Assesses application binaries for security findings. | Assessment results and the configured severity gate. |
| Enterprise App Management | Processes approved private releases and makes them available to assigned users. | Distribution results and the enterprise user catalog. |
| Google Play / App Store Connect | Receives approved store-delivery packages. | Your destination-specific store guide. |

In this documentation, My Chicken App provides a teaching example. Its tests place a demo chicken order and check the expected result. Developers review and commit the test before CI executes it. Copilot or ChatGPT can assist during authoring under the approved AI rules.

Use [Testing & Quality](../testing-quality/index.mdx) for test code, device-test requirements, and results. Use [Observability](../observability/index.mdx) for Datadog monitoring after configuring the app's telemetry.

## 4. Understand the four repositories

The app team maintains application code, tests, and the CAMP file. CAMP is the only app-owned CI/CD configuration. The enrollment request in `mobile-platform-configuration` selects the approved template ID and version. Platform Engineering maintains the versioned `bitrise.yml` and the Danger, parallel testing, Sauce Labs, NowSecure, signing, and deployment automation in `mobile-platform-configuration-bitrise-template`.

You will work with application code and enrollment configuration. Platform Engineering maintains the shared engine and workflow catalog.

| Repository | What it contains | Your first action |
|---|---|---|
| Your application repository | React Native source, Android/iOS projects, tests, and `campfile.yml`. | Run the application and its local checks. |
| `mobile-platform-configuration` | Application enrollment requests and their reviewed promotion. | Locate the approved request directory and submission procedure. |
| `mobile-platform-configuration-code` | The automation engine that validates requests and applies approved changes. | Understand its role. Platform Engineering manages execution and maintenance. |
| `mobile-platform-configuration-bitrise-template` | Catalog metadata and versioned Bitrise workflow templates. | Select a compatible, approved template and its exact version during enrollment. |

The **application starter template** generates your app's source. The **Bitrise workflow template** defines how automation builds and delivers it. The enrollment request selects the workflow template.

The latest reference places new requests at `Config/Teams/<team>/Bitrise/Apps/<app>.yaml` in the configuration repository. The team directory must match the request's `team`, and the filename must match `app_name`. An accepted request represents initial creation. Follow the reviewed continuation or reconciliation procedure for an existing application.

## 5. Confirm access before setup

Use the enterprise access process to request the access needed for your role. Use the approved Teams support channel when you need the correct repository or owner.

| Access or detail | Why you need it |
|---|---|
| Application repository | Read, change, and publish your application source. |
| Configuration repository | Submit and follow the enrollment request. |
| Approved template catalog | Confirm template status, platform, version, and allowed source branch. |
| Bitrise workspace | Inspect the enrolled application's builds, logs, and artifacts. |
| Device-test and security results | Investigate Sauce Labs test failures and NowSecure findings as permitted by your role. |
| Platform Engineering contact | Confirm protected signing bindings, platform failures, and recovery actions. |

Application teams prepare their source, tests, dependencies, and enrollment request. Use the documented support boundary to confirm which platform owner manages provisioning, protected credentials, and distribution integration for your application.

## 6. Follow the setup pages in order

Each setup page explains the working location, required inputs, commands or YAML, and the result to inspect.

| Order | Page | Result |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Prepare Your Repository | A working application revision ready for automation. |
| 2 | CAMP File Reference | Application metadata follows the confirmed schema. |
| 3 | Configuration Repository | You know where to submit enrollment configuration. |
| 4 | Enroll Your Application | The request is validated and submitted for review. |
| 5 | Review & Promote | The protected apply result and application identity are recorded. |
| 6 | Bitrise Pipelines | You understand the workflows, triggers, scripts, and artifact handoffs. |
| 7 | Danger PR Checks | Required review automation is configured and its results are understood. |
