Use **Troubleshooting & Recovery** when a stage fails or an external operation has an unknown outcome. Open [Complete Project Preview](./integrated-project-preview.mdx) to see the Android, iOS, and React Native folder and file examples. Use **Workshop Walkthrough** to practise the journey.

The [Operations Overview](./operations/index.mdx) introduces the guides covering repository inactivity, Bitrise limits and costs, template maintenance, the configuration engine, and Bitrise MCP. Open them when your task requires those topics.

## 7. Know when a release is complete

The governed routes are `qa_android`, `qa_ios`, `uat_android`, and `uat_ios`. Record the outcome of each route independently.

| Result | What you can conclude |
|---|---|
| Enrollment validation passed | The request passed its configured validation. Inspect the protected apply separately. |
| Build passed | The configured build completed. Inspect required tests, assessment, signing, and delivery evidence. |
| Artifact uploaded | The destination received the file. Follow its processing and availability results. |
| Release verified | The exact intended version is available to its approved users or testers. |

For enterprise distribution, verify the applicable signing result, enabled state, assigned audience, and exact version at the user endpoint. For store delivery, follow the destination-specific verification and approvals in [App Store & Distribution](../app-store-and-distribution/index.mdx).

