**`mobile-platform-configuration` stores requests that platform automation processes.** You add a YAML file to request a new Bitrise application. Reviewers inspect that change before protected automation applies it.

Your application source stays in its own repository. The enrollment request points to that repository and selects an approved build template.

**Work location — the `mobile-platform-configuration` checkout on your Mac.** Finish application preparation first, then obtain access to this repository through the approved enterprise process.

## 1. Understand the repositories

The app team maintains application code, tests, and the CAMP file. CAMP is the only app-owned CI/CD configuration. The enrollment request in `mobile-platform-configuration` selects the approved template ID and version. Platform Engineering maintains the versioned `bitrise.yml` and the Danger, parallel testing, Sauce Labs, NowSecure, signing, and deployment automation in `mobile-platform-configuration-bitrise-template`.

| Repository | What it contains | How you use it |
|---|---|---|
| Your application repository | Application source, native projects, tests, and CAMP metadata. | Develop the app and record the source branch and commit. |
| `mobile-platform-configuration` | Enrollment YAML and reviewed publication-reconciliation manifests. | Submit the application request and follow its review results. |
| `mobile-platform-configuration-code` | The Python automation engine and Vela integration. | Understand what processes the request. Engine maintenance belongs on the configuration-engine operations page. |
| `mobile-platform-configuration-bitrise-template` | Approved versioned Bitrise workflow templates and their metadata. | Select the exact compatible template ID and version during enrollment. |

