## 7. Know where YAML and shell scripts run

YAML declares the configured operations. A Script step executes the commands under its `content` input on the runner. In the supplied example, the shell executes `npm install -g saucectl`, waits for it to finish, then executes `saucectl --version`.

A checked-in `.sh` file must be present in the checkout and invoked by a configured step. Its directory and command must match the approved workflow. Writing the file alone leaves its execution to that workflow configuration.

Workflows running on separate VMs need configured artifact or output handoffs. A file or environment variable created in one VM requires an approved transfer mechanism before another workflow can consume it. The Parallel Testing page covers this handoff.

